Z||000004||DaRkLoRD||11-13-2000||01:40 AM||||I've been thinking.. there should be a different name for modded or stock performance imports, as many aren't even close to the fake VTEC stickered, huge winged, coffeecan exhaust'd civics etc...<P>unless you just want to call them "imports" or "sport compact cars"..... but that's no fun.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>   <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>   <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A><p>[This message has been edited by DaRkLoRD (edited 11-13-2000).]||||reg||2
Z||000005||BroCar 87||11-13-2000||01:50 AM||||Hey guys... lets not forget, there IS a difference between "ricers" and imports. Ricers are pretty much FAKES. <BR>For instance, Say a 1998 Acura Integra comes up next to you with a couple tacky stickers stating what he has in his engine/truck (ex. JL Audio or Moroso). There is NOTHING wrong with that! He is just simply telling everyone what he DOES have. <P>NOW... If a 1998 honda civic sedan comes up to you with TYPE R stickers and other stickers of engine mods/stereo mods  that he DOES not have, that is "RICEY". <P>ALSO, for you older guys (hehe   no offese) WHAT WAS THE COOL THING TO PUT ON YOUR 69 Camaro or 72 cuda??? stickers right???!!!(even though they were in the window, not on the panels as much as todays cars) Whether they be "hedman headers" or "cherry bomb exhaust" It was the cool thing to do! <BR>TO SHOW WHAT YOU HAVE UNDER/IN YOUR MUSCLE CARS!<P>And the reason that we refer to the "imports" as ricers, is because domestic car owners usually aren't (but some do!) the ones with the stickers. Imports are!<P>Just my $.02, but who has to listen??? No one!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Signature2.jpg">  <BR>87 Coupe "IRON BEAST"<BR>   Custom dual side exit exhaust!||||reg||6
